"section_type":"normalPoster"},{"data":[{"items":[],"id":19568,"title":"","description":"2","card_type":"comments","type":"comments","url":"","style":null,"length":0,"continue_watching_progress":0}],"id":0,"title":"Comments","section_type":"comments"}],"post_info":{"genres":["Drama"],"id":19568,"type":"SERIES","title":"Ashita, mama ga inai","logo":"","image":"https://cdn6.albox.co/storage/disk44/seasons/9e36214d-c036-4af3-bdaf-4bce61baea99.jpg","background_image":"https://cdn6.albox.co/storage/disk46/seasons/91ef1458-d620-48ac-aab6-1d62c89ac3e6.jpg","likes":13,"dislikes":0,"views":2137,"release_date":"1389744000000","season_number":1,"description":"Maki’s mother commits assault and Maki is temporarily placed in the children’s orphanage, Kogamo no Ie. Post is a young girl who reigns as the leader at Kogamo no Ie. While she has lost her parents, she is remarkably strong, resilient and positive. There is also Piami and Bonbi who respect Post. These girls, who each have different backgrounds, do not appear sad and seem quite indifferent. When asked for the reason for the queer nicknames they call each other, Post replies that they have cast away everything they received from their parents including their pasts as well as their names. Even if they constantly think about their parents, there will be no happiness. She advises Maki to leave the past behind. Bravado is the only weapon to protect themselves in this harsh, cold world. However, Maki believes that her mother will come to get her.","rating":{"sources":[{"title":"IMDb","logo":"https://a7.pnghunt.com/preview/450/662/555/computer-wallpaper-text-brand-yellow-imdb.jpg","max_value":10,"value":8.5}],"value":8.5,"age":"PG-13"},"current_season_id":8221,"content_control":"NORMAL"}}